{"chunk_id": "d694c1f314e8", "text": "This section transitions from the rise of Jarasandha to the plan for his downfall. After King Vrihadratha renounces worldly life and dies in the forest, Jarasandha becomes a powerful ruler who subdues many kings. His hostility toward Krishna grows after Kansa\u2019s death, and his immense strength is illustrated when he hurls a mace from Girivraja toward Mathura. With his formidable allies Hansa and Dimvaka, he is considered nearly invincible. Krishna then proposes a strategy to Yudhishthira: Jarasandha cannot be defeated in open war but may fall in single combat. Krishna supplies strategy, Bhima the strength, and Arjuna the support. Trusting Krishna\u2019s judgment, Yudhishthira consents. Disguised as Brahmanas, the three heroes depart for Magadha, their mission to kill Jarasandha and free the captive kings so that the Rajasuya sacrifice can proceed.\nKrishna proposes a covert plan for Bhima to defeat the invincible Jarasandha, and Yudhishthira approves as the three heroes set out in disguise.\nThemes: strategy and diplomacy, heroic alliance, fate of Jarasandha, prelude to Rajasuya, disguise and infiltration", "vector": [-0.00023345595400314778, -0.017250150442123413, 0.002768749836832285, 0.0164178479462862, 0.007041014730930328, 0.019438302144408226, -0.0239891204982996, -0.010638711974024773, -0.025828242301940918, -0.013162469491362572, 0.024646908044815063, 0.0002821188245434314, 0.003302363445982337, 0.006685272324830294, -0.008571378886699677, -0.0001871003769338131, 0.040541209280490875, -0.007081287447363138, 0.035762179642915726, -0.018176423385739326, 0.011303211562335491, -0.024123363196849823, -0.0023979053366929293, 0.008182075805962086, -0.027680786326527596, 0.03750733286142349, 0.016860848292708397, -0.010269545018672943, -0.00162685033865273, -0.0033678067848086357, 0.0009757746011018753, -0.0007303626625798643, -0.003691666526719928, 0.004540749825537205, -0.026365211233496666, 0.004903204273432493, 0.0083968